# 02 — Behavior safety

<!-- GEN: Why: a "simplification" that changes behavior is an unreviewed feature change. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rules S2, S3, S10, S11 with the workspace's real checks and protected boundaries (validation, error mapping, authorization, DI, contracts). -->

## Before editing

Read the callers ({{caller_lookup}}), side effects, error paths, lifecycle and the tests that cover the code.

## Must stay identical

Inputs · outputs · raised errors and messages · side effects · ordering · state transitions · accessibility behavior · performance constraints.

Existing tests pass **unchanged**; the only allowed test edit is an import path after a move.

## One step at a time

After each simplification run: `{{check_commands}}`.

## Never

- Change a test to make the simplification pass.
- Remove validation, error mapping, authorization checks, DI boundaries or package contracts ({{protected_examples}}).
- Leave a wrapper, alias or re-export after moving code ({{no_wrapper_link}}).

